{"id": "oracleanalyticsdesktop", "name": "Oracle Analytics Desktop", "category": "other", "doc": "Oracle Analytics Desktop is a desktop application for preparing, exploring and visualizing data. When a dataset is created, it profiles each column and detects its semantic type, either from value patterns (dates, US Social Security numbers, credit card numbers, email addresses, North American phone numbers, US addresses) or from the reference data shipped with the product (names and codes of countries and states, county and city names, ZIP codes). It also recognizes first-name and last-name columns. The detected types drive its recommendations to enrich, split, concatenate, mask or delete columns. A column gets a type when at least 85% of its values match it.", "website": "https://docs.oracle.com/en/middleware/bi/analytics-desktop/bidvd/data-profiles-semantic-recommendations.html", "supported_types": ["date", "usssn", "bankcard", "email", "nanpphone", "address", "country", "usstate", "uscounty", "city", "uszipcode", "person_firstname", "person_surname"], "num": 13}
{"id": "piicatcher", "name": "PII Catcher", "category": "pii", "doc": "PIICatcher is a scanner for PII and PHI information. It finds PII data in your databases and file systems and tracks critical data.", "website": "https://github.com/tokern/piicatcher", "supported_types": ["email", "birthday", "gender", "nationality", "person_fullname", "person_firstname", "lastname", "username", "password", "address", "usssn"], "num": 11}
{"id": "presidio", "name": "Microsoft Presidio", "category": "pii", "doc": "Presidio (Origin from Latin praesidium protection, garrison) helps to ensure sensitive data is properly managed and governed. It provides fast identification and anonymization modules for private entities in text such as credit card numbers, names, locations, social security numbers, bitcoin wallets, US phone numbers, financial data and more.", "website": "https://github.com/microsoft/presidio", "supported_types": ["bankcard", "date", "email", "ipaddr", "usssn", "phone", "bankaccount", "abaroutingnum", "aumedicarenum", "auabn", "auacn", "autfn", "uspassport", "usitin", "usdeanumber", "usdriverlic", "sgnric", "usbankaccount", "esnif", "bip32addr", "p2pkhaddr", "p2shaddr", "p2wpkhaddr", "p2wshaddr", "wifaddrcomp", "wifaddruncomp", "uknhsnum"], "num": 27}
{"id": "scrubadub", "name": "scrubadub", "category": "pii", "doc": "Remove personally identifiable information from free text. Sometimes we have additional metadata about the people we wish to anonymize. Other times we dont. This package makes it easy to seamlessly scrub personal information from free text, without compromising the privacy of the people we are trying to protect.`", "website": "https://github.com/LeapBeyond/scrubadub", "supported_types": ["email", "phone", "birthday", "bankcard", "postindex", "address", "person_fullname"], "num": 7}
{"id": "sherlock", "name": "Sherlock", "category": "detector", "doc": "Sherlock is a deep learning model from the MIT Media Lab that predicts the semantic type of a table column from its values, without using the column header. It was trained on 686,765 columns of the VizNet corpus whose headers matched one of 78 semantic types taken from DBpedia properties, such as city, birth Date or isbn. Many of these types are header words rather than value types, such as code, type or rank. The registry records that carry a Sherlock type in mappings.sherlock are listed here. The code and the trained model are released under the MIT license.", "website": "https://sherlock.media.mit.edu", "supported_types": ["address", "age", "birthday", "birthplace", "brand", "category", "city", "comment", "continent", "country", "currency", "dc_creator", "dc_publisher", "description", "duration", "elevation", "filesize", "gender", "genre", "industry", "isbn", "language", "name", "nationality", "orgname", "person_fullname", "religion", "species", "weight", "year"], "num": 30}
{"id": "snowflake", "name": "Snowflake sensitive data classification", "category": "pii", "doc": "Sensitive data classification in Snowflake samples the columns of tables and assigns each column a native semantic category, such as EMAIL, NATIONAL_IDENTIFIER or POSTAL_CODE, with a country-specific subcategory where one exists. Each category also has a privacy category: identifier, quasi-identifier or sensitive information. Results are stored as the SEMANTIC_CATEGORY and PRIVACY_CATEGORY tags.", "website": "https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/classify-native", "supported_types": ["aadhaar", "abn", "age", "at_driver_license", "at_passport", "at_tin", "at_vnr", "au_driver_license", "au_postcode", "auabn", "auacn", "aumedicarenum", "aupassport", "autfn", "bankaccount", "bankcard", "be_driver_license", "be_passport", "bg_driver_license", "bg_egn", "bg_passport", "birth_year", "birthday", "bsn", "ca_bank_account", "ca_postcode", "cadriverlic", "capassport", "caprovince", "casin", "ch_postcode", "city", "country", "cy_driver_license", "cy_id_card", "cy_passport", "cy_tin", "cz_driver_license", "cz_passport", "cz_rc", "de_passport", "dedriverlic", "depersonalausweis", "dk_driver_license", "dk_passport", "dkcprnum", "ee_driver_license", "ee_ik", "ee_passport", "email", "es_dni", "es_nss", "esdriverlic", "esnif", "espassport", "fi_driver_license", "fi_passport", "fiidcard", "fr_driver_license", "fr_nif", "frcni", "frnir", "frpassport", "gender", "geopoint", "gr_amka", "gr_driver_license", "gr_id_card", "gr_passport", "gr_vat", "hr_driver_license", "hr_oib", "hr_passport", "hu_driver_license", "hu_passport", "hu_personal_id", "hu_taj", "hu_tin", "iban", "icd10", "ie_driver_license", "ie_passport", "ie_pps", "imei", "in_driver_license", "in_epic", "in_gstin", "ipaddr", "it_codicefiscale", "it_driver_license", "it_passport", "jobtitle", "jp_postcode", "lab_test", "latitude", "longitude", "lt_asmens", "lt_driver_license", "lt_passport", "lu_driver_license", "lu_matricule", "l